+- `'json'`: Parse `filter` as JSON. A value that is not valid JSON stays a string:
+
+```js
+import queryString from 'query-string';
+
+queryString.parse('?filter=%7B%22a%22%3A%5B1%2C2%5D%7D&bad=%7Bnope', {
+	types: {
+		filter: 'json',
+		bad: 'json',
+	},
+});
+//=> {filter: {a: [1, 2]}, bad: '{nope'}
+```
+
+Note: The `'json'` type uses `JSON.parse`, so integers above `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` are rounded without warning (for example, 64-bit IDs). Put such values in the URL as strings.
